lly without signs of external lobulation. They are located on the left and right in the retroperitoneal space, and in adult humans are about 12 centimetres in length. They receive blood from the paired renal arteries; blood exits into the paired renal veins. Each kidney is attached to a ureter, a tube that carries excreted urine to the bladder."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-kidney"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidney"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Rassolnik","dish/rassolnik"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Brine","ingredient/brine"],["Kidneys as food","ingredient/kidneys-as-food"],["Liver as food","ingredient/liver-as-food"],["Pearl barley","ingredient/pearl-barley"],["Pickled cucumber","ingredient/pickled-cucumber"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d6/Blausen_0592_KidneyAnatomy_01.png/500px-Blausen_0592_KidneyAnatomy_01.png","w":500,"h":375,"by":"BruceBlaus. When using this image in external sources it can be cited as: Blausen.com…","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blausen_0592_KidneyAnatomy_01.png"}},"dish/walleye-sandwich":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/walleye-sandwich","n":"Walleye sandwich","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["The walleye sandwich is an important part of Minnesotan and Canadian cuisine. It consists of a fried walleye fillet, on a burger bun or hard roll, it can also include lettuce, tomato, red onions, mayonnaise or tartar sauce. The sandwich originated in Minnesota, but is now popular throughout the Upper Midwest and Eastern Canada. Walleye sandwiches are offered across the state of Minnesota."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-walleye-sandwich"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walleye_sandwich"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Canadian cuisine","cuisine/canadian-cuisine"],["Minnesotan cuisine","cuisine/minnesotan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Walleye","ingredient/walleye"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Kitchen Frau: Canadian Food","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kitchenfrau.com","note":"Canadian food section of an Alberta-based home cooking blog.","url":"https://www.kitchenfrau.com/canadian-food/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Canadian cuisine","links":[["All-dressed","dish/all-dressed"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Fritter","dish/fritter"],["Macaroni and cheese","dish/macaroni-and-cheese"],["Oasis Drive-In","dish/oasis-drive-in"]]}]}}